[{:seon.task/name "each-run-teaches-the-next"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-21 (DECISIONS: every live run better than the last): learn from every attempt automatically, without regressions, slowdown or growth. Found by hand on the first DeepSeek agent on Seon's code (`seon.reconcile/a-refused-spawn-is-recorded`): 8 turns, 59 errors, no fix; the causes were readable only by querying its branch's evaluation records: `clojure.repl/source` failing for platform vars, `slurp` of repository files not found, guessed namespaces. Extend what exists, add nothing beside it: `seon.learn/waste` already charges an attempt's wasted forms to the context producer that led to them and the judge records it (`:seon.end/waste`, `seon.reconcile/judge-tx`, class `:waste` in `seon.problems`). Make that record answer \"what did this attempt lack\": its failed forms grouped by kind (an unresolved var or namespace, no source, file not found, a contract refusal, a wrong arity), each kind with its count and one example form, and the names it tried to read that its context did not show. Then rank across attempts: `my.root/problems` (or the report it reads) answers the lacks of every attempt on main aggregated by kind, most frequent first, with one example each, so the next fix is the commonest gap across real tasks (owner: no matrix of reruns of the same tasks; a steady stream of new real tasks). Also: the server's `seon.turn/context-block` passes `:gaps-before` like the turn loop does, so outside agents stop seeing every pre-existing uncontracted function as a contract gap; and the agent's instructions (the help page, `docs/agent.md`) name today's functions (`my.schema/register!`, `source`), each resolving. Budget: about 120 net src lines; no new namespace; nothing added to the turn's hot path beyond the fold that already runs at the attempt's end."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.learn-test/an-attempt-records-what-it-lacked
                      seon.problems-test/lacks-are-ranked-across-attempts
                      seon.context-test/the-server-context-shows-only-new-contract-gaps}}]
